From f21e5cb13b2f58caaaae4ee7c2d9d6ea9596083e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: HampterDev <131729366+HampterDev@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 23:58:26 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Zero the reserved field of the map-entry packet

enter_map builds CZ_ENTER2 (0x0436) on the stack and never assigns the
four bytes after the auth code, so the login path sends whatever the
stack held there. The 2022-04-06 executable also leaves them unset, and
Hercules reads the client tick from offset 18 and skips offset 14, so
the field has no known meaning. The game-mode sender in
mode_connection.c already zero-initializes its copy of the packet.

Zero-initialize the packet and name the field reserved.

Validation: the new test_map_enter_packet runs the extracted enter_map
over stack memory filled with three marker values and checks all 23
bytes sent; offset 14 was nonzero without the fix. Release build without
warnings; the full behavioral suite passed on the completed series.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VaQB81YtRGLtH8zvfX7WTY
